<title>USA: S&amp;P says no imminent upgrade for Russia sovereign.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says no imminent upgrade for Russia sovereign.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rating agency Standard and Poor's said on Wednesday it had no immediate plan to lift Russia's sovereign credit rating.</p>
<p>Speaking in a teleconference on Russia, Helena Hessel, director of East Europe at S&amp;P, denied market speculation that an upgrade was imminent.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not plan to upgrade Russia,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The BB-minus rating on Russia's long-term foreign currency debt was assigned in October 1996 with a stable outlook.</p>
<p>Hessel said factors that constrain the rating, including a short economic track record and persistent difficulty in raising revenues, have remained unchanged since the initial assignment was made.</p>
<p>(( -- NA Treasury Desk - 212-859-1674))</p>
